<title>THAILAND: Thai sugar vessel movements on Jan 6.</title>
<headline>Thai sugar vessel movements on Jan 6.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Independent surveyors detailed Thai sugar freight movement as follows (in tonne tel quels):</p>
<p>Vessel		Position	     Quantity    Destination</p>
<p>Oun Chong Nyon Ho    N/A		 2,175	  North Korea</p>
<p>Kapitan Isirul     ETR Dec 28	  15,300	 Japan</p>
<p>Yon Pung Ho	  ETA Dec 30	  12,000	 Sri Lanka</p>
<p>Botsman Moshkov    ARRD Dec 12	 12,000	 Russia</p>
<p>Kapitan Shevchenko ETD Jan 01	  13,000	 Japan</p>
<p>Bangkhuntien	 ETD Jan 03	   4,000	 Indonesia</p>
<p>Pakarti Sembilan   ETR Jan 02	   5,250	 Indonesia</p>
<p>Pichai Samut	 ETA Jan 08	  18,000	 Japan</p>
<p>Pitak Samut	  ETR Jan 01	  14,300	 Japan</p>
<p>Ivan Makarin	 ETA Jan 01-02     17,850	 Japan</p>
<p>Great Concert	ETR Jan 02	  13,200	 Indonesia</p>
<p>Kum Gang	     ARRD Dec 21	 12,000	 Indonesia</p>
<p>Bangpo		 L/CAN Jan 02-07    2,300	 Indonesia</p>
<p>Ais Mamas	    ETD Jan 05	  13,300	 S.Korea</p>
<p>Feng Yang	    ETA Jan 04	  13,000	 Sri Lanka</p>
<p>Alam Tenaga	  ETA Jan 08	  15,000	 Malaysia</p>
<p>Bangramard	   ETA Jan 03	   6,000	 Indonesia</p>
<p>Rong Jiang	   ETA Jan 03	  12,000	 Indonesia</p>
<p>Billion		ETA Jan 08	   7,200	 Indonesia</p>
<p>Kapitan Bakanov    ETA Jan 02	  13,100	 Japan</p>
<p>Ya Giang	     ETA Jan 05-06	4,700	 Indonesia</p>
<p>Hong QI 206	  ETA Jan 02	  18,000	 Japan</p>
<p>Kwan Mo Bong	 ETA Jan 08	   8,000	 Malaysia</p>
<p>Liberty		ETA Jan 06-10	5,000	 Vietnam</p>
<p>Galactica	    ETA Jan 10	  14,300	 Indonesia</p>
<p>Tropical Rose	ETA Jan 06-10	1,500	 Cambodia</p>
<p>Sonamai		ETA Jan 05-10	1,000	 Cambodia</p>
<p>Hui Feng	     ETR Jan 07	  10,000	 S. Korea</p>
<p>Sangthai Ceramic   ETA Jan 02	   1,000	 Singapore</p>
<p>Alam Tegus	   ETA Jan 06	  12,000	 Malaysia</p>
<p>Yong Gun Bong	L/CAN Jan 11-16    8,000	 Indonesia</p>
<p>NOTE: SLD indicates that the vessel has left, ETA = Estimated Time of Arrival, ETD = Estimated Time of Departure, ETR = Estimated Time of Readiness, L/CAN indicated period when vessels are expected in for loading or be cancelled.</p>
